From aa88fad551599ec39b18cd6b97ebf2685388a1a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 18:10:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Train B, b3 (memory axis, partial): linked exile, hideaway,
 what an effect moved; seven cards

Seven of the eighteen cards, each with every rule built and scenarios (check-cards 1621 definitions,
2538 scenarios, 0 failed): Reckless Impulse, Rundvelt Hordemaster, Sapling of Colfenor, Watcher for
Tomorrow, Siren's Ruse, Valakut Exploration, Hofri Ghostforge.

Engine pieces they use:
- Linked exile read as a selector (CR 607.2a, 406.6): `exiledWith: "self"` (script/filter.mjs), counted
  ("if there are cards exiled with this enchantment") and moved by `linked`; dig's `link`.
- Exiled face down (hideaway, CR 702.75a, 406.3): a card with no characteristics in exile, its name
  hidden from every history and projection but its lookers' (`lookers`, `exiledBy`); the hideaway
  keyword compiled to its enters trigger.
- What an effect moved, as it last existed (`movedWas`; condition `about: "moved"`, CR 608.2h):
  "if a Pirate was exiled this way".
- A token copy "of that creature" with abilities added (CR 707.9a): copyPermanent `except.addAbilities`
  (compiled), the exiled card bound as it is made; `asItLastWas` for a creature that was a copy.
- "This creature or another Goblin you control dies": `self` read against last known information.
- A remembered card's printed power and toughness off the battlefield (Sapling).
- An ability on the stack keeps its source's last known information once it leaves (CR 113.7a).
- Dormant, built but no kept card uses them yet: chooseCard `random`, `among: "those cards"`, exile;
  condition `searched`; moveZone `transformed` (CR 712.14a); `power.lessThan: "self"`.

Not defined here (in progress, reverted): Advanced Reconstruction, Conspiracy Theorist, Currency
Converter, Laelia, Mizzix's Mastery, Quintorius Loremaster, Settle the Wreckage, Claim Jumper,
Coalition Relic, Fable of the Mirror-Breaker, Legion Warboss. No new suite yet.

Suites green: engine-cards, engine-compile, engine-rules-conformance, engine-projection,
engine-room-games, data-integrity, feature-wiring.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0117w9NgFp5PywoLmnpLsKQf
